#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:9
msgid "Decide how to sync GitHub repository settings with Terraform"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:11
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:13
msgid ""
"The parent story [#513](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-"
"wasm/issues/513) ships a Terraform project that declares the GitHub "
"repository settings for `tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm` (branches, protection "
"rules, labels, collaborators, Actions secrets, etc.) using the "
"`integrations/github` provider. Declaring the resources in HCL is only "
"half the work; the other half is the *workflow* that keeps the live "
"GitHub settings in sync with that declaration. Today the settings are "
"configured through the GitHub UI, which is unversioned, unreviewable, and"
" easy to drift. We need to decide how `terraform plan` and `terraform "
"apply` are run, where Terraform state lives, how the GitHub token is "
"supplied, how drift is reconciled, and who is allowed to apply — so that "
"repository configuration is versioned, reviewable, reproducible, and "
"recoverable after accidental UI changes. Which sync workflow should we "
"adopt?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:15
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:17
msgid ""
"**Reviewability of settings changes**: Every change to repository "
"settings must go through a PR so it is reviewable and bisectable, the "
"same way code changes do. This is a knock-out criterion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:18
msgid ""
"**No long-lived secrets in CI**: The CI workflow must not rely on a long-"
"lived personal access token (PAT) stored as a repository secret if a "
"short-lived, scoped alternative exists. Least-privilege authentication is"
" a knock-out criterion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:19
msgid ""
"**Blast-radius control**: A bad `terraform apply` can lock maintainers "
"out of the repository, delete branches, or wipe protection rules. The "
"workflow must make it hard to apply blindly and easy to recover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:20
msgid ""
"**Drift detection**: Manual changes made through the GitHub UI must be "
"detectable so they can be reconciled (reverted or imported) before they "
"silently diverge from the declared state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:21
msgid ""
"**Zero-cost / GitHub-native tooling**: The project is open-source and "
"community-driven; the sync workflow must not require paid services (e.g.,"
" Terraform Cloud paid tier, an external state backend with hosting costs)"
" beyond GitHub Actions and the repository itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:22
msgid ""
"**Maintainer ergonomics**: A single maintainer must be able to run the "
"workflow end-to-end without a platform team or external coordinator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:23
msgid ""
"**State durability and recoverability**: Terraform state must survive CI "
"runner termination and be restorable after state corruption or accidental"
" deletion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:25
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:27
msgid ""
"**CI `plan` on PR + local `apply` by maintainer, state in repo (committed"
" `terraform.tfstate`)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:28
msgid ""
"**CI `plan` on PR + CI `apply` on merge with OIDC, state in GitHub "
"Actions artifact**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:29
msgid ""
"**CI `plan` on PR + CI `apply` on merge with stored PAT, state in a "
"remote backend (S3/GCS/Terraform Cloud)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:30
msgid "**Scheduled `plan`-only drift check in CI + local `apply`, state in repo**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:31
msgid ""
"**Terraform Cloud / HCP Terraform managed workspace (plan + apply "
"hosted)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:33
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:35
msgid ""
"Chosen option: \"CI `plan` on PR + local `apply` by maintainer, state in "
"repo (committed `terraform.tfstate`)\", because it satisfies every knock-"
"out driver with the smallest moving surface: `terraform plan` runs on "
"every PR that touches the Terraform project so changes are reviewable; "
"`terraform apply` is run locally by a maintainer after merge using a "
"short-lived PAT issued from the maintainer's own GitHub account (no long-"
"lived CI secret, no OIDC trust config to maintain); state is committed to"
" the repository as `terraform.tfstate` so it is versioned, bisectable, "
"and recoverable from Git history without an external backend or paid "
"service. The state file contains no secrets (the `integrations/github` "
"provider reads the token from the `GITHUB_TOKEN` environment variable at "
"runtime, never writes it into state), so committing it is safe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:37
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:39
msgid ""
"Good, because every settings change is reviewable in a PR — `terraform "
"plan` output is posted to the PR by CI, so reviewers see the exact diff "
"before merge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:40
msgid ""
"Good, because no long-lived CI secret is required: the maintainer runs "
"`terraform apply` locally with a PAT issued on the fly from their own "
"account, scoped to the `repo` and `admin:org` (if applicable) scopes, and"
" revoked or allowed to expire immediately after."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:41
msgid ""
"Good, because state committed to the repo is bisectable with the rest of "
"the configuration — a bad apply can be rolled back by checking out the "
"previous `terraform.tfstate` and re-running `terraform apply`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:42
msgid ""
"Good, because drift detection is free: a scheduled `terraform plan` job "
"(see [ADR-0005](0005-verify-agents-md-quality-in-ci.md) for the same "
"scheduled-CI pattern) posts a failing plan when the live GitHub settings "
"diverge from the committed state, prompting a maintainer to either import"
" the manual change or revert it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:43
msgid ""
"Good, because it is zero-cost and GitHub-native: GitHub Actions runs "
"`plan` for free on public repositories, and state in Git needs no "
"external backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:44
msgid ""
"Good, because a single maintainer can run the whole workflow without a "
"platform team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:45
msgid ""
"Bad, because `terraform apply` is not automated — a maintainer must run "
"it locally after merge, adding a manual step and a small risk that a "
"merged PR is forgotten and never applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:46
msgid ""
"Bad, because committing `terraform.tfstate` to Git scales poorly if the "
"state grows large or contains frequently-changing resources; for this "
"repo's small settings surface (branches, labels, protection rules) the "
"state file stays small and the trade-off is acceptable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:47
msgid ""
"Bad, because concurrent applies can conflict (two maintainers running "
"`terraform apply` at once); for a single-maintainer repo this is "
"negligible, but it would need a state lock (e.g., a remote backend with "
"DynamoDB locking) if the maintainer team grows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:48
msgid ""
"Neutral, because `terraform.tfstate` must be `.gitignore`-excluded for "
"any *unmanaged* Terraform scratch state but explicitly *tracked* for this"
" project — a small config discipline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:50
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:52
msgid "Compliance with this decision will be confirmed by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:54
msgid ""
"A `terraform/` project exists in the repository with `main.tf` declaring "
"the GitHub repository settings via the `integrations/github` provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:55
msgid ""
"A GitHub Actions workflow runs `terraform fmt -check`, `terraform "
"validate`, and `terraform plan` on every PR touching `terraform/**`, and "
"posts the plan output as a PR comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:56
msgid ""
"`terraform.tfstate` is committed to the repository (not `.gitignore`-d "
"for the `terraform/` project), and Git history shows it evolving "
"alongside `main.tf`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:57
msgid ""
"No PAT or token is stored as a repository secret used by the `apply` step"
" — `apply` is documented as a local-only maintainer step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:58
msgid ""
"A scheduled (e.g., weekly) GitHub Actions workflow runs `terraform plan "
"-detailed-exitcode` and opens or updates an issue when exit code "
"indicates drift (non-zero on diff)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:59
msgid ""
"The Terraform configuration and workflow are documented in a "
"`terraform/README.md` explaining the local `apply` workflow, the PAT "
"scope required, and how to reconcile drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:60
msgid ""
"The `integrations/github` provider is pinned to a specific version in "
"`main.tf`, and `terraform.lock.hcl` is committed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:62
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:64
msgid ""
"CI `plan` on PR + local `apply` by maintainer, state in repo (committed "
"`terraform.tfstate`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:66
msgid ""
"Good, because every settings change is reviewable in a PR via CI `plan` "
"output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:67
msgid ""
"Good, because no long-lived CI secret is needed — `apply` runs locally "
"with a short-lived maintainer PAT, satisfying the no-long-lived-secrets "
"knock-out criterion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:68
msgid ""
"Good, because state in Git is bisectable and recoverable from history "
"with no external backend, satisfying state durability at zero cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:69
msgid "Good, because drift detection is a free scheduled `plan` job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:70
msgid "Good, because a single maintainer can run it end-to-end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:71
msgid ""
"Neutral, because `terraform.tfstate` must be explicitly tracked for this "
"project while remaining ignored elsewhere — a small config discipline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:72
msgid ""
"Bad, because `apply` is manual; a merged PR can be forgotten and never "
"applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:73
msgid ""
"Bad, because it does not scale to large state or many concurrent "
"maintainers (no state locking)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:75
msgid ""
"CI `plan` on PR + CI `apply` on merge with OIDC, state in GitHub Actions "
"artifact"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:77
msgid ""
"See [GitHub Actions OIDC for Terraform Cloud / HCP "
"Terraform](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/tutorials/github"
"/github-actions) and [GitHub Actions: "
"OIDC](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/deployment/security-hardening-"
"your-deployments/about-security-hardening-with-openid-connect)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:79
msgid ""
"Good, because `apply` is automated on merge — no manual maintainer step, "
"no forgotten PRs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:80
msgid ""
"Good, because OIDC issues short-lived tokens with no long-lived secret, "
"satisfying least-privilege."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:81
msgid ""
"Good, because state is stored as a GitHub Actions artifact, keeping it "
"out of Git."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:82
msgid ""
"Neutral, because GitHub Actions artifacts expire (default 90 days); state"
" must be re-uploaded each run or the artifact retention must be raised, "
"adding config."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:83
msgid ""
"Bad, because GitHub Actions OIDC for the `integrations/github` provider "
"requires a GitHub App or `hashicorp/tf-action-setup` with OIDC trust "
"configured at the GitHub org/repo level — non-trivial setup for a single-"
"maintainer open-source repo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:84
msgid ""
"Bad, because state in an artifact is not bisectable with the "
"configuration and is lost if the workflow stops running before re-upload,"
" failing the state-durability driver for a low-activity repo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:85
msgid ""
"Bad, because automated `apply` on merge increases blast radius: a merged "
"PR applies immediately with no human in the loop at apply time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:87
msgid ""
"CI `plan` on PR + CI `apply` on merge with stored PAT, state in a remote "
"backend (S3/GCS/Terraform Cloud)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:89
msgid ""
"See [Terraform remote "
"backends](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/settings/backends)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:91
msgid ""
"Good, because a remote backend (S3+DynamoDB, GCS, HCP Terraform) provides"
" state locking, solving the concurrent-apply problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:92
msgid "Good, because `apply` is automated on merge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:93
msgid "Good, because state is durable and not lost with CI runner termination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:94
msgid ""
"Bad, because it requires a long-lived PAT stored as a repository secret "
"for the `apply` step, violating the no-long-lived-secrets knock-out "
"criterion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:95
msgid ""
"Bad, because an S3/GCS backend requires a cloud account with hosting "
"costs, violating the zero-cost driver. HCP Terraform's free tier has "
"limits that may not cover a public repo with many settings resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:96
msgid ""
"Bad, because it introduces external infrastructure (a cloud bucket, an "
"HCP Terraform workspace) outside the repo, increasing the moving surface "
"for a single-maintainer open-source project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:98
msgid "Scheduled `plan`-only drift check in CI + local `apply`, state in repo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:100
msgid ""
"Good, because it is identical to the chosen option for `apply` and state,"
" and adds only a scheduled `plan` job — which the chosen option already "
"includes as a drift detector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:101
msgid ""
"Neutral, because this is a strict subset of the chosen option rather than"
" a true alternative; it is folded into the decision outcome as the drift-"
"detection mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:102
msgid ""
"Bad, because considered as a standalone option it leaves PR-time `plan` "
"unspecified, weakening the reviewability knock-out criterion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:104
msgid "Terraform Cloud / HCP Terraform managed workspace (plan + apply hosted)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:106
msgid "See [HCP Terraform](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cloud-docs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:108
msgid ""
"Good, because it hosts both `plan` and `apply`, providing a UI for run "
"history, state, and approvals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:109
msgid ""
"Good, because it supports OIDC and short-lived tokens, satisfying least-"
"privilege."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:110
msgid ""
"Good, because state is managed by HCP Terraform with locking and version "
"history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:111
msgid ""
"Bad, because it introduces an external hosted service with its own access"
" control, billing, and quota — violating the zero-cost / GitHub-native "
"driver for a public repo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:112
msgid ""
"Bad, because it moves the apply decision out of the repository's PR flow,"
" reducing the \"everything travels through the same review/PR flow as "
"code\" property the repo values (see [ADR-0000](0000-use-markdown-"
"architectural-decision-records.md))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0009-decide-how-to-sync-github-repo-settings-with-terraform.md:113
msgid ""
"Bad, because the free tier has a limited number of workspaces and runs "
"per month, which may not cover sustained activity."
msgstr ""

